jkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T00:02:32Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T00:03:43Z","body":"> We should also change the return type for `String` & `CharSequence` arrays further down below the current logic from `Array` to `PackedStringArray`.\r\n\r\nI noticed a few other things going through the method:\r\n- the `case ARG_NUMBER_CLASS_BIT | ARG_ARRAY_BIT | ...` cases' return type should be updated to typed arrays corresponding to the type of the remaining `*_BIT`. They only differ from the cases without `ARG_NUMBER_CLASS_BIT` in that the java object contains wrapped versions of the primitive types (e.g: `Integer` instead of `int`)\r\n- the `case ARG_ARRAY_BIT | ARG_TYPE_CLASS` is not handled","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689382832/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691138642","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103375#issuecomment-2691138642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103375","id":2691138642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gZ4RS","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T17:02:23Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T20:05:15Z","body":"Thanks for the review!\r\n\r\nI've ended up marking this back to DRAFT again, because as I was updating this for the review above, I just couldn't deal with how inefficient most of these conversions were, and rewrote them. :-) I need to get a proper test project going to test all of these, which I haven't done yet, I've only written the code.\r\n\r\nWith regard to the efficiency changes:\r\n\r\n- In all cases, this will now allocate the Godot array at the correct size up front, rather than push each element onto the array one by one (which avoids re-allocating it numerous times)\r\n- In the cases where the Godot types match the JNI types, it will now have JNI fill up the array directly, rather than grabbing the elements one at a time. There's some cases where we can't do this, for example, we're converting Java `short[]` into `PackedInt32Array`, where `short` 